WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:08.200
Customers are everyone who has ordered, or asked for a quote,
ranked by what they have spent.

2
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.560
Add one yourself: company name, email, phone.

3
00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:15.060
Mark them a trade customer and set how they pay.

4
00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:21.200
On account means they order now and settle on terms,
instead of paying by card at the shop.

5
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.780
Now you can trade with them.

6
00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:28.880
A credit limit of £50,000. Nothing owed yet, so all of it is there to spend.

7
00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:34.160
When they pay, record it against the account and the available credit goes back up.

8
00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.200
Notes, tags and every order and enquiry they have had, all on the one record.

9
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:41.260
That is a customer account.

10
00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:45.600
Connect your own accounts system and the credit keeps itself up to date.
